.TH VDR-SUITE-BACKEND-AGENT 8 "August 2026" "VDR-Suite" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite-backend-agent \- outbound read-only Backend Agent for VDR-Suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdr-suite-backend-agent
.B --config
.I PATH
.RI [ --once " | " --rotate-credential ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Backend Agent establishes an outbound HTTPS connection to the VDR-Suite
Control Plane.  The Phase-63 foundation supports controlled enrollment,
protocol negotiation, backend-generation fencing, read-only capability
publication, heartbeat renewal and reconnect reconciliation.
.PP
It does not execute VDR mutations, expose local provider URLs, or accept an
inbound connection at the VDR site.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The packaged service reads
.IR /etc/vdr-suite/backend-agent.conf .
The file contains the Control-Plane HTTPS origin, stable Backend ID, protected
identity and enrollment paths, optional CA certificate, read-only capabilities,
timeouts and bounded reconnect delays.  It must not contain an enrollment
token or runtime credential.  Those values live only in files below
.IR /var/lib/vdr-suite/backend-agent
with mode 0600.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Read the non-secret key/value configuration from PATH.
.TP
.B --once
Perform one connect/capability/heartbeat cycle and exit.  Intended for bounded
acceptance tests.
.TP
.B --rotate-credential
Synchronize with the Control Plane, rotate the technical Agent credential,
persist the replacement atomically, reconnect with the new credential and
exit.  An interrupted rotation is reconciled from the protected identity file
without restoring the old credential after the Control Plane has committed.
.SH SECURITY
TLS peer and host verification are mandatory.  Redirects, proxy inheritance,
netrc credentials, URL user information and non-HTTPS origins are rejected.
The Agent authenticates only as its persisted technical Agent identity and is
scoped to its enrolled Backend and current backend generation.
Credential rotation is also fenced by the current Agent instance, backend
generation and credential generation.  A pending replacement is stored with
mode 0600 before dispatch so a lost response can be recovered safely.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vdr-suite/backend-agent.conf
Non-secret service configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/vdr-suite/backend-agent/identity
Mode-0600 Agent identity and runtime credential.
.TP
.I /var/lib/vdr-suite/backend-agent/enrollment
Mode-0600 one-time enrollment package, removed after successful enrollment.
.SH SYSTEMD
The packaged unit is
.BR vdr-suite-backend-agent.service (5).
It runs as user and group
.B vdr
with a read-only system view and write access limited to the Agent state
directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-backend-agent-enroll (8),
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8)
